{:edb/db-before-t 1869 :edb/db-after-t 1870 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535182 50 #inst "2026-10-08T18:52:36.626Z" 13194139535182 true] [17592186114992 1100 "Let ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/assets/38c4cba166fdfcd0954a18156946e41834a626cccee4baab976861dd23574c85.png) Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" 13194139535182 true] [17592186114992 1100 "Let $\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$, gives the result of the product $EA$." 13194139535182 false] [17592186114992 1145 "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the identity matrix and replacing the second row with the result of adding $5$ times the first row to the second row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{2} \\mid:=5R_{1} + R_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= E\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation\n\n$$\nR_2:=5R_1+ R_2\n$$\n\nto $A$." 13194139535182 false] [17592186114992 1145 "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the identity matrix and replacing the second row with the result of adding $5$ times the first row to the second row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=5{R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation $R_2:=5R_1+ R_2$ to $A.$" 13194139535182 true] [17592186114993 1100 "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation $R_1:=R_1 - R_2$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$. Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." 13194139535182 false] [17592186114993 1100 "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation $R_1:=R_1 - R_2$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." 13194139535182 true] [17592186114993 1145 "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation\n\n$$\nR_1:=R_1 - R_2\n$$\n\nto $A$.\n\nTo find $E$, we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{1} \\mid:=R_{1} - R_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= E\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA$:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139535182 false] [17592186114993 1145 "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation $R_1:=R_1 - R_2$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA\\mathbin{:}$\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/assets/a4a2b1035b3b5699ff3558ffa839fbd667ad6defaf30a158d628c7011ab97aa8.png)" 13194139535182 true] [17592186114994 1100 "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$:\n$R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2, \\qquad R_2:=R_2+3R_1$\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." 13194139535182 false] [17592186114994 1100 "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nR_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2, \\qquad  R_2:=R_2+3R_1\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." 13194139535182 true] [17592186114994 1145 "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2$. The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n$I|= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{1} \\mid ↔R_{2}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}; = E_{1}$\n- The second elementary row operation is $R_2:=R_2+3R_1$. The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n$I|= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{2} \\mid:=R_{2} + 3R_{1}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}; = E_{2}$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A$, we multiply by $E_1$ on the left and get $E_1 A$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to $E_1 A$, we multiply by $E_2$ on the left and get $E_2 E_1 A$:\n\n$$\nMissing \\end{bmatrix}\n$$" 13194139535182 false] [17592186114994 1145 "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is $R_2:=R_2+3R_1.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by $E_1$ on the left and get $E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/assets/d35cb368b7380f08e486757813138fa3f3332ed40a9b0e5faeab7a20c3119bef.png)\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to $E_1 A,$ we multiply by $E_2$ on the left and get $E_2 E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/assets/c87dbe6c81a670dd62d8a130d3085b2e9b36d5d3ad27d53bda571ec69b639689.png)" 13194139535182 true] [17592186115166 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335952 13194139535182 true] [17592186115166 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335959 13194139535182 true] [17592186115166 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335966 13194139535182 true] [17592186115166 1020 #edb/ref 17592186336036 13194139535182 true] [17592186115166 1020 #edb/ref 17592186336049 13194139535182 true] [17592186115167 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335973 13194139535182 true] [17592186115167 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335980 13194139535182 true] [17592186115167 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335987 13194139535182 true] [17592186115167 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335994 13194139535182 true] [17592186115167 1020 #edb/ref 17592186336001 13194139535182 true] [17592186115168 1020 #edb/ref 17592186336008 13194139535182 true] [17592186115168 1020 #edb/ref 17592186336015 13194139535182 true] [17592186115168 1020 #edb/ref 17592186336022 13194139535182 true] [17592186115168 1020 #edb/ref 17592186336029 13194139535182 true] [17592186115754 1017 #edb/ref 17592186113895 13194139535182 false] [17592186115754 1017 #edb/ref 17592186336043 13194139535182 true] [17592186115754 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535182 true] [17592186115754 1100 "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2 \\cdot 2$ matrix $A$:\n\n$R_{2}:=-2R_{2}, R_{1}↔R_{2}, R_{2}:=R_{2} + 3R_{1}$\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." 13194139535182 false] [17592186115754 1100 "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:=-2{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." 13194139535182 true] [17592186115754 1145 "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:=-2{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:=-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" 13194139535182 true] [17592186335952 1017 #edb/ref 17592186335953 13194139535182 true] [17592186335952 1089 "q-130838" 13194139535182 true] [17592186335952 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535182 true] [17592186335952 1100 "Let $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" 13194139535182 true] [17592186335952 1113 #uuid "c25477cb-b615-5c8d-82e5-e31fcd78f3c1" 13194139535182 true] [17592186335952 1145 "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the second row of the identity matrix and adding $-5$ times the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1}$ to $A.$" 13194139535182 true] [17592186335953 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335954 13194139535182 true] [17592186335953 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335955 13194139535182 true] [17592186335953 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335956 13194139535182 true] [17592186335953 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335957 13194139535182 true] [17592186335953 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335958 13194139535182 true] [17592186335953 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535182 true] [17592186335953 1041 "selection" 13194139535182 true] [17592186335953 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335954 13194139535182 true] [17592186335953 1110 #u